1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,145
Today is October 08, 2026.

3
00:00:07,145 --> 00:00:14,755
Overnight, the Standard and Poor's five hundred fell zero point two two percent, closing near five thousand eight hundred.

4
00:00:14,755 --> 00:00:22,292
The Nasdaq dipped zero point two two percent as well, holding three consecutive closes above previous record peaks.

5
00:00:22,292 --> 00:00:30,944
Meanwhile, the Russell two thousand dropped one point three percent, extending aggressive institutional pair trades long tech against small caps.

6
00:00:30,944 --> 00:00:37,329
Breadth deteriorated sharply, with over seventy percent of S and P constituents finishing in the red.

7
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:43,787
Only defensive sectors gained ground, led by consumer staples, healthcare, and utilities.

8
00:00:43,787 --> 00:00:52,194
In fixed income, thirty-year Treasury yields surged intraday to five point seven three percent, marking fresh twenty-four-year highs.

9
00:00:52,194 --> 00:00:59,375
Ten-year benchmark paper touched five point three five percent before paring gains after a robust Treasury auction.

10
00:00:59,375 --> 00:01:05,344
The Federal Reserve September minutes revealed unanimous support for a twenty-five basis point hike.

11
00:01:05,344 --> 00:01:15,699
Officials maintained that sticky inflation, driven by tariffs, geopolitical shocks, and massive artificial intelligence infrastructure spending, warrants tighter policy.

12
00:01:15,699 --> 00:01:22,831
The probability of an October pause stands at eighty-three percent, though another hike remains on the table before year-end.

13
00:01:22,831 --> 00:01:30,564
Geopolitical risks compounded macro anxiety as Middle East tensions pushed Brent crude past one hundred and two dollars per barrel.

14
00:01:30,564 --> 00:01:37,047
WTI crude crossed ninety dollars, reigniting concerns over headline energy inflation.

15
00:01:37,047 --> 00:01:43,591
This rising cost of capital directly collides with enterprise capital expenditure in mega-cap technology.

16
00:01:43,591 --> 00:01:51,238
Bank of America notes top ten index concentration now sits at forty-two percent, exceeding dot-com bubble levels.

17
00:01:51,238 --> 00:01:57,439
Goldman Sachs expects S and P third-quarter earnings to expand twenty-seven percent year-over-year.

18
00:01:57,439 --> 00:02:02,893
