19
00:02:02,893 --> 00:02:10,871
Ray Dalio warns that debt-financed AI infrastructure faces severe friction as corporate borrowing costs touch eight to ten percent.

20
00:02:10,871 --> 00:02:15,221
Supply chains show stark divergence across hardware layers.

21
00:02:15,221 --> 00:02:22,353
DRAM contract prices anticipate up to twenty percent price hikes, validating durable memory pricing power.

22
00:02:22,353 --> 00:02:30,160
Conversely, mechanical storage faces headline risk as TDK plans to divest its magnetic head manufacturing unit.

23
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:36,324
Turning to pivotal single stocks, Micron Technology demonstrated outstanding relative strength.

24
00:02:36,324 --> 00:02:42,451
Micron shares rallied four percent to close at one thousand and eighty-eight dollars on massive volume.

25
00:02:42,451 --> 00:02:50,711
High-bandwidth memory order books remain sold out through twenty-twenty-seven, insulating near-term cash flows from broader liquidity strain.

26
00:02:50,711 --> 00:02:55,589
Wall Street price targets range from thirteen hundred to three thousand dollars.

27
00:02:55,589 --> 00:03:02,464
Immediate resistance sits near eleven hundred and fifty dollars, with technical support anchored at one thousand dollars.

28
00:03:02,464 --> 00:03:10,564
In enterprise software, Oracle experienced significant regulatory friction over its Project Lighthouse mega data center in Wisconsin.

29
00:03:10,564 --> 00:03:21,312
State regulators rejected power transmission approvals, pushing operational online dates toward twenty-twenty-nine and increasing estimated buildout costs by seventy-five percent.

30
00:03:21,312 --> 00:03:27,513
Yet Oracle shares absorbed the headline with light volume, signaling tight institutional ownership.

31
00:03:27,513 --> 00:03:35,111
Downside support holds firmly near two hundred and ten dollars, while overhead resistance rests at two hundred and thirty dollars.

32
00:03:35,111 --> 00:03:42,672
Amazon trades near critical inflection territory amid emerging shifts in AI-driven agentic e-commerce platforms.

33
